Summary: Two ways in. A member's assistant speaks the Model Context Protocol at /api/mcp with a delegation token the member granted in Kin; it reads the verified record and may propose, never approve. A home-care agency's software reports visits at /api/v1/visits and sends invoices for them at /api/v1/invoices, signed with its key; a report is evidence beside the family's calendar, an invoice is a bill a person reviews, and neither pays anything by itself. Every payment waits for a person in Kin, with a fresh multi-factor check. PayPal's own tools stay behind Kin.
